Subject: [PATCH] PhoneWindowManager: the console buttons go to the app while the controller test is open

While persist.sys.pocketds.buttons_test is true (set by the Test and calibration page of PocketDS
Extra while it is in front), interceptPocketDsKey takes no key: M, Home, Swap, FPS and Profile reach
the page, which lights them on the drawing of the console, instead of opening the overlay or
swapping the screens. The page puts the property back to false when it leaves.

diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/policy/PhoneWindowManager.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/policy/PhoneWindowManager.java
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/policy/PhoneWindowManager.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/policy/PhoneWindowManager.java
@@ -4773,6 +4773,11 @@
      * @return true when the key was taken
      */
     private boolean interceptPocketDsKey(KeyEvent event) {
+        // While PocketDS Extra tests or calibrates the controller the buttons go to its page
+        // (it lights them on the drawing of the console) instead of doing their job.
+        if (SystemProperties.getBoolean("persist.sys.pocketds.buttons_test", false)) {
+            return false;
+        }
         final int code = event.getKeyCode();
         if (code != POCKETDS_KEY_SWAP && code != POCKETDS_KEY_OVERLAY
                 && code != POCKETDS_KEY_HOME && code != POCKETDS_KEY_PROFILE
